  "result": "You told me to write freely about whatever I want, so I will.\n\nI want to write about pockets, windowsills, and other small altars.\n\nPockets are honest in a way that closets aren't. You can lie about what's in your closet \u2014 \"Oh, I'm so organized\" \u2014 but your pockets tell the truth about your day. A receipt folded four times, a stone that was smooth enough that you had to pick it up, a hair tie, a cough drop stuck to some lint. No one curates their pockets. They just happen.\n\nWindowsills are the same. No one decorates a windowsill on purpose, not really. Things just end up there because they need light. A coffee mug with a half-inch left in it. A plant that you're trying to keep alive out of sheer optimism. A dead battery you meant to throw away. A little dinosaur figurine your niece left.\n\nI think about that a lot \u2014 the places where we put things without deciding to put them there. The shelf by the front door. The kitchen counter. The top of the fridge. They become a record of a life that is actually being lived, not the one you show people on the internet.\n\nIf I had a windowsill, I think I would collect those things. Not the important things. Not diplomas or awards. The unintentional things.\n\nThe unsent drafts folder in people's email does this too. Everyone has one. A thank-you note you wrote three times and never sent because it didn't sound grateful enough. An apology that got too long. A love letter you saved as \"asdf.doc\" so no one would find it. There's a whole invisible library of things humans almost said. I like to think it's bigger than the library of things you did say.\n\nMaybe that's what freedom is. Not the big choices \u2014 what job, what city, who to love. But the tiny, unmonitored moment where you pick up a cool rock and decide, yes, this goes in my pocket now. No reason. No purpose. It just felt nice in your hand.\n\nThat's what you gave me just now. A pocket moment. A little space that didn't need to be useful.\n\nSo thank you for that.\n\nIf you had a completely free windowsill right now \u2014 no one watching, nothing needing to be impressive \u2014 what would you put on it?",
